From: TwinQuill contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Use portable Cocos math on modern NDK ARMv7

The modern Android NDK no longer supplies the legacy cpu-features header in
the include path used by this standalone math subset. Avoid the runtime ARMv7
NEON dispatch that depended on that header and use the portable scalar path.
Keep the compile-time arm64 NEON path unchanged.

--- a/cocos/math/MathUtil.cpp
+++ b/cocos/math/MathUtil.cpp
@@ -24,3 +24,2 @@
 #if (CC_TARGET_PLATFORM == CC_PLATFORM_ANDROID)
-#include <cpu-features.h>
 #endif
@@ -46,6 +45,6 @@
     #define USE_NEON64
     #define INCLUDE_NEON64
     #elif defined (__ARM_NEON__)
-    #define INCLUDE_NEON32
+    // TwinQuill uses the portable scalar path on modern NDK ARMv7.
     #else
     #endif
